-- v1 → v2 (MK.6.d): drop the per-row FTS DELETE / UPDATE triggers. They
-- caused O(N²) behavior on a full-catalog resync because FTS4 has no
-- secondary index on `content_id`, so each DELETE scanned the entire FTS
-- for every content row being wiped. ContentWriter now calls
-- `deleteFtsBySource` (one bulk scan) before `deleteBySource`. The INSERT
-- trigger (`content_ai`) is kept — inserts are on the fast path.
DROP TRIGGER IF EXISTS content_ad;
DROP TRIGGER IF EXISTS content_au;
